        "lastModifiedBy": null
      },
      "text": {
        "content": "<h1>Phase 3 &mdash; The Cast</h1><p><em>Every named Phase 3 NPC with committed art, one to a page, alphabetical. Use it to put a face to a name mid-scene without opening four journals.</em></p><p><strong>Showing a face to the table.</strong> Click the portrait itself and use <em>Show Players</em> from the image popout &mdash; that shares the picture alone. Do <em>not</em> share the page: the text under each portrait is written for you, not for them.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Who</th><th>In one line</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Ailen Moraven</strong></td><td>Tamsin Moraven's daughter, nineteen, has been living quietly in Hardby since her mother's disappearance.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Anver \"Tarsh\" Resh</strong></td><td>The intermediary who hired Merev Sarth.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Berrin Onn</strong></td><td>Mid-fifties vault clerk at the C&amp;V Hardby branch.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Castrian Vell</strong></td><td>Trina Alvere's Hardby contact, social host for the Commercial Cover party.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Dren Marsh</strong></td><td>Former harbor-watch corporal, now sleeping guard at the C&amp;V Hardby branch.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Edrin Saetar</strong></td><td>Sculptor master in the Salters' Quarter.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Hella Voren</strong></td><td>Veska Maelan's apprentice scribe at the Quay clearing-house.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Hesren Vesh</strong></td><td>The Loftwick satellite's one bonded clerk, taken down to Hardby within days of the party's visit to Wick Lane and parked in a senior post on paper with nothing to do in it.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Joren Krill</strong></td><td>Hardby weighmaster, on Cindren &amp; Vhal's payroll.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Mira Cindren</strong></td><td>Veshen Cindren's cousin and the C&amp;V Hardby junior partner who handles official delegations.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Olfard</strong></td><td>Barkeep at the Coopered Wreck on the Hardby waterfront.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Olo Crask</strong></td><td>Retired Aerdi marine captain hired to guard the recovery target.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Reyna Worth</strong></td><td>Cindren-aligned overseer who runs a daily check at the third bell.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Sarro Pell</strong></td><td>Widow housekeeper for Castrian Vell, eleven years' service.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Solen Mereth</strong></td><td>The compromised senior clerk of the Hardby branch.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Tamsin Moraven</strong></td><td>The rescued captive whose disappearance triggers Phase 2 and 3.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Vella Tannin</strong></td><td>Sympathetic clerk at the C&amp;V Hardby branch.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Veska Maelan</strong></td><td>Caelith Dunivar's Hardby contact.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Yorra Mel</strong></td><td>Master of the Lacquer Wave, a Hardby-flagged wool trader working the long coast to Rel Astra. No firm ties, no questions; files bales, not names.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Zoria Weis</strong></td><td>A debt Caelith is calling, not a friend.</td></tr></tbody></table>",
        "format": 1,
        "markdown": null
      }
    },
    {
      "_id": "BR2P3PoPgAilenMorav",
      "_key": "!journal.pages!BR2P3PortraitJr.BR2P3PoPgAilenMorav",
      "name": "Ailen Moraven",
      "type": "text",
      "title": {
        "show": false,
        "level": 1
      },
      "sort": 200000,
      "ownership": {
        "default": -1
      },
      "flags": {},
      "_stats": {
